  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💄 Makeup Brand Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a makeup or cosmetics line, from Pout of Office to Delaunay Beauté."
    },
    "intro": "Good makeup brand names are short and say something about the look: playful like <em>Hue Knew</em>, minimal like <em>Studio Stain</em>, or French and luxurious like <em>Rouge Doré</em>. Launching a lip gloss line, an indie palette brand or a clean-beauty range? This **makeup brand name generator** gives you cosmetics brand names in eight styles, and you can check each one is free before you order packaging.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good makeup brand names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Hue Knew</strong>: a pun on who knew, with a colour word built in.</li><li><strong>Wing &amp; a Prayer</strong>: a pun for an eyeliner brand: anyone who's done a winged flick knows the feeling.</li><li><strong>Lip Bunny</strong>: cute and short, for a lip gloss line.</li><li><strong>Studio Stain</strong>: minimal and modern, for tints and stains.</li><li><strong>Rouge Doré</strong>: French for \"golden red\", for a luxury feel.</li><li><strong>Lavender Glaze</strong>: an aesthetic name for dewy, glossy products.</li><li><strong>Sea Buckthorn Beauty</strong>: a plant name for a clean or natural range.</li><li><strong>Sarah Rouge</strong>: a founder name with a beauty word. Put your own name in the box.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How makeup brands are named",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Founder names</strong> are a long tradition in beauty, from Helena Rubinstein to Estée Lauder, and suit a personal brand.</li><li><strong>French</strong> sounds expensive: <em>beauté</em> is beauty, <em>rouge</em> red, <em>doré</em> golden.</li><li><strong>Product words</strong> like <em>pout</em>, <em>kohl</em>, <em>glaze</em> and <em>flush</em> tell people what you sell.</li><li><strong>Clean beauty</strong> has no legal definition, so a name like <em>Barefaced Beauty</em> sets a mood rather than making a claim.</li><li><strong>The rules:</strong> in the UK, every cosmetic needs a safety assessment by a qualified assessor, a UK Responsible Person, and notification through the government's Submit Cosmetic Product Notification service before it goes on sale.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
